# Slice 346 (the author 2026-11-10, LMX_blog/2026-11-10.md#colon-declares-not-assigns): `Struct1: Struct2` is a
# declaration, not an assignment. The repeated declaration gives the place Struct1 the newly declared Structure -- its
# q w e r t are gone, no second field Struct1 arises -- and Struct1 holds the Structure Struct2 itself, under its own
# name, with its a, b, c. The three lines are the author's example.
Struct2: a b c
Struct1: q w e r t
Struct1: Struct2
